<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Second United Front</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1937">1937</a>–<a href="/years/1945">1945</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Second United Front was the alliance between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuomintang">Chinese Nationalist Party</a> (Kuomintang) and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chinese-communist-party">Chinese Communist Party</a> against the Japanese invasion, formed in 1937 after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xian-incident">Xi'an Incident</a> of December 1936. The Communists placed their forces under nominal Nationalist command as the Eighth Route Army and New Fourth Army, and their base became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaan-gan-ning-border-region">Shaan-Gan-Ning Border Region</a>. Cooperation broke down after the New Fourth Army Incident of 1941, and civil war resumed after 1945.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/second-united-front.jpg" alt="Second United Front" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 中華民國國防部 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Republic_of_China_Army.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
